  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Health Security Strengthening Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is an Official Development Assistance (ODA) funded UKaid project from the Department of Health and Social Care (DHSC)&#x2019;s Global Health Security Programme. In 2021/22 DHSC provided &#xa3;312,00 from its ODA budget to the Global Health Security Strengthening Project. Public Health England (PHE) delivered the project and contributed a further &#xa3;128,000 of non-ODA funding. The project provided the resources and technical expertise to increase PHE engagement on global health security at international level, complementing and building on existing in-country work. It shared learning and knowledge from other PHE activity on global health security and sought to expand and strengthen engagement with global organisations, initiatives and partnerships. This project was not put out to an open, competitive tender process because Public Health England (now the UK Health Security Agency (UKHSA)) was an executive agency of DHSC with a mandate to deliver on pandemic preparedness and therefore exempt from the tender process as it was within DHSC&#x2019;s body of expertise.</narrative>
  </description>
